%I A398950 #9 Aug 15 2026 07:57:30
%S A398950 1,3,11,13,15,17,19,29,31,33,35,37,39,51,53,55,57,65,67,69,83,85,87,
%T A398950 89,91,93,101,103,105,107,109,111,127,129,137,139,141,155,157,159,161,
%U A398950 163,177,179,181,183,191,193,195,197,199,201,209,211,213,215,217,219
%N A398950 Numbers k such that k, k+2, and k+4 are all squarefree.
%C A398950 All the terms are odd since every pair of consecutive even numbers contains one multiple of 4, which is not squarefree.
%C A398950 The asymptotic density of this sequence is (1/2) * Product_{p odd prime} (1 - 3/p^2) = 2 * A206256 = 0.250973961811618596668... .
%H A398950 Amiram Eldar, <a href="/A398950/b398950.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..10000</a>
%e A398950 1 is a term since 1, 3, and 5 are all squarefree.
%t A398950 q[k_] := q[k] = SquareFreeQ[k]; Select[Range[1, 219, 2], q[#] && q[# + 2] && q[# + 4] &]
%o A398950 (PARI) isok(k) = if(!(k % 2), 0, issquarefree(k) && issquarefree(k+2) && issquarefree(k+4));
%Y A398950 Subsequence of A005117, A056911 and A069977.
%Y A398950 Cf. A007675, A206256.
%K A398950 nonn,easy
%O A398950 1,2
%A A398950 _Amiram Eldar_, Aug 15 2026
